# Shell scripts must reach a runner with LF endings whatever the checkout does.
# `verify` runs gate-views.sh through git-bash on Windows, and a CRLF line ending
# arrives as a stray carriage return at the end of every command, which fails in
# a way that names nothing useful.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The published cost page and the readings it is built from.
#
# `npm run verify` regenerates the page and fails if it differs from the
# committed copy, which is what stops a number being edited into it. The
# generator writes LF, and this machine checks out CRLF by default, so without
# these two lines that check would go red on a fresh Windows clone for a reason
# nobody could act on.
docs/benchmark.md text eol=lf
docs/measurements/*.json text eol=lf
